    "result": "I implemented `encode` and `decode` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`. I haven't run or tested anything, since shell access wasn't available.\n\n`encode` finds each maximal run of a character. A run of 4 or more becomes `~n~c`. A shorter run is written out as itself, except that each `~` is doubled to `~~`.\n\n`decode` reads left to right. It treats `~~` as one `~` and `~n~c` as `c` repeated `n` times. It accepts only ASCII digits in the count. It raises `ValueError` in each case the spec lists:\n- a `~` at the end of the text;\n- a `~` followed by something other than `~` or a digit;\n- a count with leading zeros;\n- a count below 4;\n- a count not followed by `~`;\n- a missing character after the second `~`.",
